<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<MECA ID = "T100001A500A748" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "11Mar2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Warning Function</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Because of its convenience, the Smart Entry &amp; Start System may cause the driver to become unaware of the key. As a result, problems such as "not noticing that the electronic key has been taken outside the cabin (taken out by a passenger)", "the driver exiting the vehicle with the engine running" and "the driver exiting the vehicle with the shift position in a position other than "P"" may occur.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>The warning function prevents these problems by warning the driver and passengers with the meter display, the built-in single-tone buzzer in the meter and the wireless answer-back buzzer before such situations arise.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740010b" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "4.375in" />
</FIGURE>
